WHAT IS A GOOGLE ADS AUDIT? (Detailed Explanation Card)

A Google Ads Audit is a comprehensive review of your Google Ads account, campaigns, 
keywords, ads, landing pages, and settings to identify:

✓ Performance issues (why some campaigns underperform)
✓ Budget waste (money spent on irrelevant keywords)
✓ Missed opportunities (profitable keywords you're not bidding on)
✓ Configuration errors (tracking not set up correctly)
✓ Quality Score issues (lowering your ad rank)
✓ Ad copy problems (not compelling enough)
✓ Landing page optimization gaps

Think of it like a "health checkup" for your Google Ads account.

THE AUDIT PROCESS (Step-by-Step):

STEP 1: "Account Structure Review"
✓ Are campaigns organized properly?
✓ Is budget allocation strategic?
✓ Are campaign settings optimized?
✓ Is ad rotation set correctly?

STEP 2: "Keyword Analysis"
✓ Which keywords bring conversions?
✓ Which keywords waste money?
✓ Are there negative keywords missing?
✓ Is keyword match type appropriate?
✓ What keywords are you NOT bidding on?

STEP 3: "Ad Performance Analysis"
✓ Which ad copies perform best?
✓ What's your average Click-Through Rate (CTR)?
✓ Are headlines compelling?
✓ Are call-to-action (CTA) buttons clear?
✓ Is ad relevance score high?

STEP 4: "Landing Page Review"
✓ Does landing page match ad promise?
✓ Is page load speed fast?
✓ Is it mobile-friendly?
✓ Are CTAs clear and visible?
✓ Is form too long (causing abandonment)?

STEP 5: "Conversion Tracking Verification"
✓ Is tracking pixel installed correctly?
✓ Are all conversions being tracked?
✓ Is conversion value set up?
✓ Can we attribute revenue to clicks?

STEP 6: "Competitive Analysis"
✓ What are competitors bidding on?
✓ What keywords are you missing?
✓ How do your ads compare?

STEP 7: "ROI & Budget Analysis"
✓ How much are you spending vs. earning?
✓ What's your cost per conversion?
✓ Which keywords are most profitable?
✓ Where should you increase/decrease budget?

WHAT IS OPTIMIZATION? (Definition)
Optimization is taking the insights from the audit and IMPLEMENTING changes to improve 
performance. It's the action step.

